n two arguments are allowed.\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```lua\nprintx(bit.bxor(0xa5a5f0f0, 0xaa55ff00))  --> 0x0ff00ff0\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/bit-lua#bit.bxor:x1-x2...)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:bit.bxor","jsName":"bxor","line":120,"member":"bxor","modulePath":["bit"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"number","optional":false,"rawName":"x1","rawType":"number"},{"description":"number(s)","optional":false,"rawName":"...","rawType":"number"}],"rawName":"bit.bxor","returnDescriptions":["y bitwise xor of the provided arguments"],"returns":["number"],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/bit.lua"},{"description":"Returns the bitwise logical left-shift of its first argument by the number of bits given by the second argument.\nLogical shifts treat the first argument as an unsigned number and shift in 0-bits.\nOnly the lower 5 bits of the shift count are used (reduces to the range [0..31]).\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```lua\nprint(bit.lshift(1, 0))              --> 1\nprint(bit.lshift(1, 8))              --> 256\nprint(bit.lshift(1, 40))             --> 256\nprintx(bit.lshift(0x87654321, 12))   --> 0x54321000\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/bit-lua#bit.lshift:x-n)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:bit.lshift","jsName":"lshift","line":139,"member":"lshift","modulePath":["bit"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"number","optional":false,"rawName":"x","rawType":"number"},{"description":"number of bits","optional":false,"rawName":"n","rawType":"number"}],"rawName":"bit.lshift","returnDescriptions":["y bitwise logical left-shifted number"],"returns":["number"],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/bit.lua"},{"description":"Returns the bitwise left rotation of its first argument by the number of bits given by the second argument. Bits shifted out on one side are shifted back in on the other side.\nOnly the lower 5 bits of the rotate count are used (reduces to the range [0..31]).\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```lua\nprintx(bit.rol(0x12345678, 12))   --> 0x45678123\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/bit-lua#bit.rol:x-n)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:bit.rol","jsName":"rol","line":154,"member":"rol","modulePath":["bit"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"number","optional":false,"rawName":"x","rawType":"number"},{"description":"number of bits","optional":false,"rawName":"n","rawType":"number"}],"rawName":"bit.rol","returnDescriptions":["y bitwise left-rotated number"],"returns":["number"],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/bit.lua"},{"description":"Returns the bitwise right rotation of its first argument by the number of bits given by the second argument. Bits shifted out on one side are shifted back in on the other side.\nOnly the lower 5 bits of the rotate count are used (reduces to the range [0..31]).\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```lua\nprintx(bit.ror(0x12345678, 12))   --> 0x67812345\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/bit-lua#bit.ror:x-n)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:bit.ror","jsName":"ror","line":169,"member":"ror","modulePath":["bit"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"number","optional":false,"rawName":"x","rawType":"number"},{"description":"number of bits","optional":false,"rawName":"n","rawType":"number"}],"rawName":"bit.ror","returnDescriptions":["y bitwise right-rotated number"],"returns":["number"],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/bit.lua"},{"description":"Returns the bitwise logical right-shift of its first argument by the number of bits given by the second argument.\nLogical shifts treat the first argument as an unsigned number and shift in 0-bits.\nOnly the lower 5 bits of the shift count are used (reduces to the range [0..31]).\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```lua\nprint(bit.rshift(256, 8))            --> 1\nprint(bit.rshift(-256, 8))           --> 16777215\nprintx(bit.rshift(0x87654321, 12))   --> 0x00087654\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/bit-lua#bit.rshift:x-n)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:bit.rshift","jsName":"rshift","line":187,"member":"rshift","modulePath":["bit"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"number","optional":false,"rawName":"x","rawType":"number"},{"description":"number of bits","optional":false,"rawName":"n","rawType":"number"}],"rawName":"bit.rshift","returnDescriptions":["y bitwise logical right-shifted number"],"returns":["number"],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/bit.lua"},{"description":"Normalizes a number to the numeric range for bit operations and returns it. This function is usually not needed since all bit operations already normalize all of their input arguments.\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```lua\nprint(0xffffffff)                --> 4294967295 (*)\nprint(bit.tobit(0xffffffff))     --> -1\nprintx(bit.tobit(0xffffffff))    --> 0xffffffff\nprint(bit.tobit(0xffffffff + 1)) --> 0\nprint(bit.tobit(2^40 + 1234))    --> 1234\n```\n\n(*) See the treatment of hex literals for an explanation why the printed numbers in the first two lines differ (if your Lua installation uses a double number type).\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/bit-lua#bit.tobit:x)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:bit.tobit","jsName":"tobit","line":206,"member":"tobit","modulePath":["bit"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"number to normalize","optional":false,"rawName":"x","rawType":"number"}],"rawName":"bit.tobit","returnDescriptions":["y normalized number"],"returns":["number"],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/bit.lua"},{"description":"Converts its first argument to a hex string. The number of hex digits is given by the absolute value of the optional second argument. Positive numbers between 1 and 8 generate lowercase hex digits. Negative numbers generate uppercase hex digits. Only the least-significant 4*|n| bits are used. The default is to generate 8 lowercase hex digits.\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```lua\nprint(bit.tohex(1))              --> 00000001\nprint(bit.tohex(-1))             --> ffffffff\nprint(bit.tohex(0xffffffff))     --> ffffffff\nprint(bit.tohex(-1, -8))         --> FFFFFFFF\nprint(bit.tohex(0x21, 4))        --> 0021\nprint(bit.tohex(0x87654321, 4))  --> 4321\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/bit-lua#bit.tohex:x-n)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:bit.tohex","jsName":"tohex","line":225,"member":"tohex","modulePath":["bit"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"number to convert","optional":false,"rawName":"x","rawType":"number"},{"description":"number of hex digits to return","optional":true,"rawName":"n","rawType":"number"}],"rawName":"bit.tohex","returnDescriptions":["s hexadecimal string"],"returns":["string"],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","semanticOverride":{"evidence":{"claim":"The second argument is optional and defaults to 8.","line":128,"observed":"lua_isnone(L, 2) ? 8 : (SBits)barg(L, 2)","source":"engine/script/src/bitop/bitop.c","sourceSha256":"98b344b9d460859c9bfbfeb640c652242f8b823b5080494f63b381c11da1c5eb"},"parameterOptional":{"n":true}},"source":"doc/bit.lua"}],"types":[{"description":"","disposition":"generated-type","fields":[],"kind":"class","line":12,"name":"defold_api.bit","source":"doc/bit.lua"}]}}